# Algodue UPM215/310/3060.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Algodue UPM215 / UPM310 / UPM3060 — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: algodue-upm-upt-modbus-protocol.pdf (Rev. 010, 03/09/2010)
# | - Covers: UPM215 (DIN rail), UPM310 (DIN 96×96), UPM3060 (DIN 144×144).
# | - 3-phase (or single-phase configurable) power quality meters.
# | - FC03 (Read Holding Registers) for all registers listed here.
# | - Two register banks:
# | - Raw integer bank at 0x0000: 64-bit integers (4 registers), milli-units.
# | - IEEE float bank at 0x1000: IEEE 754 f32 (2 registers), same milli-units.
# | - This TOML uses the IEEE float bank (0x1000 = 4096 decimal).
# | - All values stored in milli-units: mV→V, mA→A, mW→W etc. → scale=0.001.
# | - Energy in mWh, mvarh, mVAh → scale=0.001 for Wh/varh/VAh.
# | - Factory defaults: slave=1, 9600 baud, 8N1/E1.
# | - (*) = option-dependent register.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Algodue
@model=UPM215/310/3060
@vendor_website=algodue.com
@description=3-phase power quality meter — V/I/P/Q/S/PF/COSφ/THD/frequency/energy/demands (f32 milli-units, FC03, 0x1000 IEEE float bank). Covers UPM215, UPM310, UPM3060.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/algodue-upm215-310-3060.toml; Source: algodue-upm-upt-modbus-protocol.pdf (Rev. 010, 03/09/2010). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
